ALVA — Intelligent Combat, Combo Assist & Controller UI Update

Primary objective

Carefully implement a major combat responsiveness and accessibility update in the Alva repository:

https://github.com/hiyroscript/alva

This update has five interconnected requirements:

1. Introduce a new Combo assist setting, enabled by default.
2. Implement intelligent player-requested move interruption and cancellation.
3. Display each attack’s artwork beside its name in Controller Controls.
4. Fix Combat Assist being cancelled or bypassed when Run is held while attacking.
5. Fix Combat Assist inconsistently failing immediately after another move.

The most important requirement is intelligent, predictable combat behavior.

The system must understand the difference between repeating the current attack, requesting a different attack, attacking during recovery, attacking during cooldown, and holding a movement direction.

Do not implement simplistic logic that cancels every animation whenever an input is detected.

Do not sacrifice existing gameplay mechanics to make these features work.

